# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# claudeDM — .gitignore
#
# READ THIS BEFORE REORGANISING data/.
#
# Everything under data/ falls into exactly one of two groups, and the rules
# below are written per-directory to keep them apart:
#
#   PRODUCT (committed) — the game itself, identical for every player:
#       data/campaigns/**   campaign.json + scenarios/*.json
#       data/defaults/**    starting characters and NPCs, incl. the .jpg
#                           portraits that sit beside the .json
#       data/rules/**       races, classes, spells, monsters, ...
#
#   PLAY DATA (never committed) — anything the running server writes about a
#   person. It is personal data; the directory names alone are derived from
#   email addresses (server/player-data.js: emailToSlug):
#       data/players.json          account records incl. password hashes
#       data/players/<slug>/...    that person's character library
#       data/sessions/<uuid>/...   session.json, archive.jsonl, transcripts
#       data/chat/YYYY-MM-DD.json  party chat archives
#       data/dm-settings/<slug>.json and data/dm-settings.json
#       data/characters/...        pre-campaign layout, kept for migrations
#
# There is deliberately NO blanket `data/` or `data/**` rule. A blanket rule
# would silently stop new campaigns from being committed and nobody would
# notice until a campaign went missing from a fresh clone. Ignore directories
# one at a time, and when you add a directory that the server writes into,
# add it here in the same commit.
#
# Style note: each play-data directory is ignored as `dir/*` (its contents),
# not `dir/`, so the noDelete.txt / .gitkeep placeholders below can be
# re-included. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, so `dir/` would make those negations silently do nothing.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE CANNOT DO: it does not touch history. data/players.json —
# email addresses and unsalted SHA-256 password hashes — is present in 11
# commits already in this repository, and .gitignore has no effect on commits
# that already exist. Those records come back with every clone and every
# checkout of an old commit. Removing them means rewriting history, which the
# board considered and decided against; see the incident record
# 2026-08-31-claudedm-player-data-in-git-history. Treat those hashes as
# disclosed to anyone who has ever cloned this repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Build artefacts and tooling -------------------------------------------
node_modules/
client/node_modules/
client/dist/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Scratch directories used during development.
tempola/
work/


# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# No secret belongs in this repository, not even briefly.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key


# --- Play data: accounts and credentials ------------------------------------
# The account store: email, display name, unsalted SHA-256 password hash, role.
# Written by server/routes/players.js and server/bot/bot-accounts.js.
data/players.json

# Belt and braces: any file called players.json, anywhere in the tree. This is
# the one file that has already leaked, so it is worth the small cost that a
# future campaign may not use that filename for product content.
players.json

# Bot-farm configuration (self-play harness). Creates real accounts.
data/bot-config.json


# --- Play data: per-player character libraries ------------------------------
# data/players/<email-derived slug>/<campaign>/characters/*.json
# and, for the bot harness, <campaign>/sessions/*.json.
# The slug is a reversible transform of an email address, so the directory
# NAMES are personal data too, not only the file contents.
data/players/*
# The app expects data/players/ to exist in a fresh clone; the placeholder is
# what makes an empty directory survive a clone, so it stays committed.
!data/players/noDelete.txt
!data/players/.gitkeep


# --- Play data: sessions ----------------------------------------------------
# data/sessions/<uuid>/session.json, archive.jsonl, characters/, npcs/.
# session.json holds the full transcript of everything anyone typed.
data/sessions/*
!data/sessions/noDelete.txt
!data/sessions/.gitkeep


# --- Play data: party chat --------------------------------------------------
# data/chat/YYYY-MM-DD.json — one file per day of out-of-character chat.
data/chat/*
!data/chat/.gitkeep
!data/chat/noDelete.txt


# --- Play data: DM settings -------------------------------------------------
# Per-player overrides, one file per account, named from the email slug.
data/dm-settings/*
!data/dm-settings/.gitkeep
!data/dm-settings/noDelete.txt
# Instance-wide DM settings, edited at runtime by an admin. This is deployment
# state, not product. The committed template lives at
# data/defaults/demo/dm-settings.json, which this anchored rule does not match.
data/dm-settings.json


# --- Play data: legacy flat character directory -----------------------------
# Pre-campaign layout. Empty apart from its placeholder, but migration scripts
# still write here, so keep it ignored rather than deleting the rule.
data/characters/*
!data/characters/noDelete.txt
!data/characters/.gitkeep


# --- Crash debris -----------------------------------------------------------
# writeJsonAtomic (server/json-recovery.js) writes <file>.tmp-<pid>-<rand>
# next to its target and renames it. A crash mid-write leaves these behind,
# including inside data/campaigns/ and data/defaults/.
*.tmp-*
